"answer": "Project Zenith is a high-priority initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and leveraging AI for data visualization. Key milestones include a kick-off in Q3 2023 (June/July) with a lead team including Sarah Tan and Marcus Cole. The project has received significant budget approvals, starting with $500,000 for Phase One, increasing to $55,000 for compliance, and a final executive approval of $2M covering R&D and marketing. Progress updates highlight breakthroughs in predictive analytics and the successful completion of the testing phase. The project involves gathering R&D ideas by July 20th, seeking stakeholder feedback by the end of November, and implementing updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year. Celebrations and meetings are scheduled for October 10th and November 20th."
